        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/israel-steps-up-attacks-in-lebanon-amid-fallout-with-us-over-iran-deal",
        "orario": "11:27",
        "timestamp": 1781861279,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel steps up attacks in Lebanon amid fallout with US over Iran deal Middle East Issued on: 19/06/2026 - 11:27 Modified: 19/06/2026 - 11:28 Israel’s military said on June 19 its forces struck targets throughout southern Lebanon overnight as Hezbollah reported intense fighting in the area, threatening the nascent agreement between Iran and the United States to end their war. Israel and Hezbollah are not parties to the agreement, but Iran insists Israel must withdraw from south Lebanon. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky tells us more from Jerusalem. US-Iran peace negotiations abruptly called off amid growing criticism 19/06/2026 Middle East Iran says Trump agreed to deal terms 'out of desperation' as US Democrats blast agreement 19/06/2026 Americas Replay: US VP JD Vance defends Iran-US agreement and FRANCE 24's analysis 18/06/2026 Middle East For Israel, US-Iran deal a 'disaster' incompatible with its security interests 18/06/2026 Middle East As a result of Iran war, Gulf states 'diversifying defensively' 18/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran agreement leaves Israelis 'in profound state of shock' 18/06/2026 Middle East Face-to-face signing of US-Iran deal 'up in the air' after Trump's Versailles signing 18/06/2026 Middle East Kept outside of negotiations, can the US-Iran deal bring peace to Lebanon? 18/06/2026 Middle East Tehran comes out as the 'winner' of the initial US - Iran deal 18/06/2026 Middle East"
